    "created_at": "2026-08-04T14:58:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-04T14:58:36Z",
    "body": "Diagnosed \u2014 ComfyUI core, not this node pack. When the text encoder gets offloaded/staged by the new memory management (typical on \u226412 GB cards), `cast_bias_weight` intentionally hands back an already-dequantized bf16 weight \u2014 but the quantized-Embedding path in `comfy/ops.py` still routes int8_tensorwise weights into the int8 gather kernel, which requires int8 input: hence `No backend can handle 'dequantize_int8_embedding'`. The int8 *Linear* path has exactly the guard this path is missing. FP8 TEs take a different branch, which is why `qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled` works.\n\nWorkarounds until it's fixed upstream: the fp8_scaled TE, or enough free VRAM that the TE isn't staged. Filing upstream with a proposed fix; will link it here.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
